/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  transport01 -- THE TRANSPORT CORRELATIONS, AS OBJECTS THAT PROVE THEMSELVES.

  NOTHING IN THIS CASE IS MEASURED.  Read that first.  Choupo's catalogue
  carries no measured gas viscosity, thermal conductivity or diffusivity,
  so no number below is compared with an experiment.  What the case shows
  is what CAN be shown without one, and it says which kind each check is:

    THEORY      an identity kinetic theory or the correlation's own author
                supplies -- Eucken on a monatomic gas MUST give the
                Chapman-Enskog lambda = (15/4) R mu / M exactly; Wilke's
                phi_ii MUST be 1 for identical species.  A wrong constant
                fails here.
    ARITHMETIC  the correlation's own closed form at a stated point,
                written as a literal -- Chung's Neufeld Omega at T* = 1,
                Fuller at round numbers, Sato-Riedel at T = Tb where its
                bracket ratio is 1 by construction, the fitted liquid forms
                reducing to Andrade.  This checks the TRANSCRIPTION and the
                units, and the output says so rather than letting 0.0000 %
                read as a validation.

  WHAT THE RUN DOES, IN TWO PARTS.
  (1) VERIFY.  Every registered model in five families, plus the shared
      gas mixing rule, reproduces its own anchor; each prints its window,
      its PRIMARY citation and the anchor's kind.
  (2) COMPARE.  N2, O2, CO2 and water vapour at 373.15 K, 1 bar: every
      registered gas-viscosity and gas-conductivity model for every
      component, each with its computable window verdict (Chung's T*
      against the Neufeld domain; Eucken's "polyatomic" by the record's own
      Cp), then the case's mixing rules -- Wilke for mu, Wassiljewa /
      Mason-Saxena for k -- at the equimolar composition (announced).

  WHAT TO READ IN THE OUTPUT.  Three things.
    * The spread across models is 0.00 % -- for BOTH gas families -- and
      the bench says why: ONE model is registered per family.  A spread
      over one is not agreement; Chapman-Enskog (Lennard-Jones sigma and
      eps/k, which no record carries yet) is the named next member.
    * Chung ANNOUNCES, for each of the four components, that Vc was
      estimated from Zc(omega) and that the polar and association terms
      were dropped.  Water is polar; the announcement is the only thing in
      the run that says the non-polar form was applied to it anyway.
    * Eucken flags CO2 and water (and, by their Cp, N2 and O2 -- diatomics
      are polyatomic) as APPROXIMATION HERE, because plain Eucken is exact
      only for a monatomic gas and this case has none.

  WHAT THIS CASE DOES NOT DO.  It does not say which model is right, and
  it does not compare with a measurement.  The golden pins that the
  anchors, the values and the (absent) spread have not MOVED -- nothing
  more.  Record: docs/design/transport-correlations-as-objects.md.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

operations
(
    {
        name     bench;
        type     transportBench;
        //  373.15 K, 1 bar: warm, dilute, well inside every gas window, so
        //  the only verdicts that fire are the ones about the MODELS
        //  (Eucken's polyatomic approximation), not about the state.
        compare
        {
            T   373.15 K;
            P   1 bar;
        }
    }
);
